# COPY THIS INTO YOUR REPO ROOT ALONGSIDE factory/.
#
# Not tidiness. If this repository is ever checked out on Windows with core.autocrlf on,
# every factory/*.sh gets CRLF, and on the Linux box that actually runs the factory each
# one fails with:
#
#     bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M
#
# which reads as "the file is missing". You will look for a path bug for an hour.
#
# Pinned here, in the repo, so it does not depend on anyone's local git config - the
# machine that breaks is never the machine you are sitting at.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
